{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011PAWQFxVjwuenBM5nRgop5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental temperature dependence NMR density\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The dynamics of liquid 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate measured with implanted-ion $^8$Li $\\\\beta$-NMR\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.03684\"},{\"title\":\"ecs.confex.com\",\"url\":\"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/imlb2016/webprogram/Paper76763.html\"},{\"title\":\"dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in/items/8ed4634f-035a-4192-822c-4f03ec20d341/full\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion in Molten Lithium Nitrate\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........d6d6807597b1fec9872b396fc4495643\"},{\"title\":\"link.aps.org\",\"url\":\"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302\"},{\"title\":\"Application Note 17\",\"url\":\"https://nmr.oxinst.com/assets/uploads/X-Pulse_App_Note_17_Measuring_diffusion_at_different_temperatures_using_NMR_with_pulsed_field_gradients_WEB.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.rsc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.rsc.org/suppdata/d3/cp/d3cp04666d/d3cp04666d1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Open Access Article\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2023/ra/d3ra02094k\"},{\"title\":\"explore.cnr.it\",\"url\":\"https://explore.cnr.it/resource/item/440695\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"}]\n\nThe search did not find experimental data on liquid elemental lithium self-diffusion, its temperature dependence, or its density. The results were about other systems:\n\n- **Molten lithium nitrate:** A 1992 study measured ⁷Li⁺ self-diffusion by NMR spin-echo with pulsed field gradients over 537–615 K. It found that the self-diffusion coefficient depends on the isotopic composition and shows a maximum at equimolar ratio. This is a salt, not liquid Li metal.\n- **Solid lithium:** A 1975 paper by Messer and Noack reported ⁷Li spin-lattice relaxation in solid lithium versus temperature and frequency, which relates to self-diffusion. It is not a liquid-phase measurement.\n- **Other results** covered lithium electrolytes, ionic liquids, and garnet-type conductors, which are not relevant to liquid lithium metal.\n\nFor the liquid-metal values, I'd suggest searching for Li-7 NMR or tracer diffusion studies of liquid lithium near its melting point (about 454 K), and for a reference density table such as NIST or liquid-metal property compilations. I can run another search on those if you want.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5dc4987-72c0-45ec-afbc-d6f69c780717","uuid":"21f6f88d-ad5f-4623-babf-54e309194d2c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:12:44.221Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental temperature dependence NMR density","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0113Zusp8Tw5m7SJmCtmHfiF","content":[{"title":"The dynamics of liquid 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate measured with implanted-ion $^8$Li $\\beta$-NMR","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.03684"},{"title":"ecs.confex.com","url":"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/imlb2016/webprogram/Paper76763.html"},{"title":"dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in","url":"https://dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in/items/8ed4634f-035a-4192-822c-4f03ec20d341/full"},{"title":"Self-Diffusion in Molten Lithium Nitrate","url":"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........d6d6807597b1fec9872b396fc4495643"},{"title":"link.aps.org","url":"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302"},{"title":"Application Note 17","url":"https://nmr.oxinst.com/assets/uploads/X-Pulse_App_Note_17_Measuring_diffusion_at_different_temperatures_using_NMR_with_pulsed_field_gradients_WEB.pdf"},{"title":"www.rsc.org","url":"https://www.rsc.org/suppdata/d3/cp/d3cp04666d/d3cp04666d1.pdf"},{"title":"Open Access Article","url":"https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2023/ra/d3ra02094k"},{"title":"explore.cnr.it","url":"https://explore.cnr.it/resource/item/440695"},{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"}]},"The search did not find experimental data on liquid elemental lithium self-diffusion, its temperature dependence, or its density. The results were about other systems:\n\n- **Molten lithium nitrate:** A 1992 study measured ⁷Li⁺ self-diffusion by NMR spin-echo with pulsed field gradients over 537–615 K. It found that the self-diffusion coefficient depends on the isotopic composition and shows a maximum at equimolar ratio. This is a salt, not liquid Li metal.\n- **Solid lithium:** A 1975 paper by Messer and Noack reported ⁷Li spin-lattice relaxation in solid lithium versus temperature and frequency, which relates to self-diffusion. It is not a liquid-phase measurement.\n- **Other results** covered lithium electrolytes, ionic liquids, and garnet-type conductors, which are not relevant to liquid lithium metal.\n\nFor the liquid-metal values, I'd suggest searching for Li-7 NMR or tracer diffusion studies of liquid lithium near its melting point (about 454 K), and for a reference density table such as NIST or liquid-metal property compilations. I can run another search on those if you want."],"durationSeconds":4.742413756999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011PAWQFxVjwuenBM5nRgop5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
