{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1DmQb1xE67zJRzbCMB7Yy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium density and self-diffusion coefficient vs temperature handbook (Ohse, Murday Cotts, Lowenberg)\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Helium bubbles in liquid lithium: a potential issue for ITER\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.00293\"},{\"title\":\"Density fluctuations and single-particle dynamics in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0005149\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"m.math-net.ru\",\"url\":\"https://m.math-net.ru/eng/tvt693\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"peeref.com\",\"url\":\"https://peeref.com/works/14514882\"},{\"title\":\"m.math-net.ru\",\"url\":\"https://m.math-net.ru/eng/ftt11863\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up the Ohse, Murday/Cotts, or Lowenberg handbook data tables directly, but it did surface several related sources.\n\n- **Murday and Cotts (1968):** The classic experimental self-diffusion study of liquid lithium appears in reference lists as *J Chem Phys* 48:4938–4945 Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945. A 2012 paper says its simulated values agree well with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure.\n- **Ohse:** Reference lists cite Ohse's work on self-diffusion and isotope effects in liquid lithium (*Philos Mag*, 1986 and 2006) Ominia M (1986) Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium. Philos Mag 54:561–576; Ominia M (2006) Self-diffusion and inter-diffusion coefficients of liquid lithium isotopes. The name is spelled \"Ominia\" in these listings, so the Ohse attribution is unconfirmed by this search.\n- **Lowenberg:** I found no source mentioning Lowenberg.\n- **Density:** An older NASA correlation fits liquid lithium density linearly against temperature, giving p = 562 - 0.100 T, with density in kg/m³ and T in kelvin. It was built from experimental data and is meant for temperatures up to about 1600 K.\n- **Diffusion vs. temperature:** Recent work reports that self-diffusion increases with temperature and decreases with pressure, and it fits an Arrhenius form to its simulation results. A neutron-scattering study covered 500–830 K.\n\nFor the actual tabulated values, you'd need the original Murday–Cotts paper or the Ohse handbook chapter itself, which this search didn't reach.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5dc4987-72c0-45ec-afbc-d6f69c780717","uuid":"46da0170-94aa-4b07-ba4d-8f59418f82ab","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:12:55.140Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium density and self-diffusion coefficient vs temperature handbook (Ohse, Murday Cotts, Lowenberg)","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KtuXU4AbDQC4vzYZEN8cs1","content":[{"title":"Helium bubbles in liquid lithium: a potential issue for ITER","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.00293"},{"title":"Density fluctuations and single-particle dynamics in liquid lithium","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0005149"},{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"s002