reases with temperature and decreases with pressure, and it fits an Arrhenius form to its simulation results. A neutron-scattering study covered 500–830 K.\n\nFor the actual tabulated values, you'd need the original Murday–Cotts paper or the Ohse handbook chapter itself, which this search didn't reach."],"durationSeconds":6.346107636000005,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E1DmQb1xE67zJRzbCMB7Yy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
